Two independent cycles (a <-> b, c <-> d) and a node (e) that depends on
a. Breaking the first cycle used to leave a stale entry in the dependents
map, so a node that was already emitted went back into the ready set. The
sort then emitted it again, never reached the remaining nodes, and could
loop forever. Every file must appear exactly once.

  $ for m in a b c d e; do
  >   case $m in
  >     a) ref=B;; b) ref=A;; c) ref=D;; d) ref=C;; e) ref=A;;
  >   esac
  >   printf '[@@@css ".%s{color:red;}"]\nlet _ = %s.x\n' $m $ref > $m.ml
  > done

  $ styled-ppx.generate a.ml b.ml c.ml d.ml e.ml
  styled-ppx: dependency cycle among c.ml, d.ml; dropping the edge from d.ml to c.ml to keep a deterministic order
  styled-ppx: dependency cycle among a.ml, b.ml; dropping the edge from b.ml to a.ml to keep a deterministic order
  /* This file is generated by styled-ppx, do not edit manually */
  .d{color:red;}
  .c{color:red;}
  .b{color:red;}
  .a{color:red;}
  .e{color:red;}
